{"title":"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When fifteen is written in numeric form, it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>When the following number is written in numeric form, what is the sum of its digits?\n</p>\n<center>two million five hundred sixty-four thousand fourteen</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without writing out the number, we can notice that the sum would be:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d61a44c13d3cc764f08bc3edf631f09b2513875d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 5 + 6 + 4 + 1 + 4 = 7 + 10 + 5 = \\boxed{22}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"326\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>This is because the two million part has a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the five hundred sixty-four thousand part has a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55e33fef045b62992a5976f2578f5740ad567392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 6 + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, and the fourteen part has a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/163fb61a1020bd660a0bcf1bdce0d5cab4fdbe93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> with the digits.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC\">2023 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_3\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 3\">Relay B Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_2\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 2\">Relay C Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Pro